# Rule 2 — Scan toward 30, then apply what was found

**Scan target:** Prefer collecting up to **30 preference-matched** jobs before apply.

- Phase 1: open All Filters, apply prefs, scan/scroll and **auto next-page** until `matched >= 30` or pages/search plan are exhausted. **Never ask** the user to click “Next page”.
  - Tell the user apply has **not** started yet: wait until 30 jobs match (~1 minute). Keep `matched/30` visible (panel status, notice, toast).
- Phase 2: apply the queued matches one by one with a **short settle** (not full humanPace slowdown).
  - Navigate **job → next job** — do not return to the search list between applies.
  - Cap `betweenJobs` (~0.6–1.2s). Skip read pauses and the 2-minute session break during the batch.
  - If `matched >= 30`, apply the batch of 30.
  - If scan exhausts with `0 < matched < 30`, **still apply** every match found — do not block apply on a full 30.
  - If `matched === 0`, do not apply; report that nothing matched.
- When the session finishes, ask **Apply more** or **Close — view dashboard**. Close must close the Naukri work tab and open the Cosmo dashboard (reuse an existing Cosmo tab when possible). Do not prompt for another Next page.
- Never invent extra result pages past real pagination while filling the batch.
- Single Naukri work tab only.
